vaulthalla (1.12.2-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Identities
    - identities::Manager owns one canonical User/Group object per id and
      publishes immutable states into it (atomic shared_ptr); readers take one
      state per check, user+group views are coherent across a publication.
    - Identity and RBAC writes (users, groups, memberships, vault role
      assignments, overrides, role templates) commit, reload what they touched
      in one snapshot and publish before returning; ops/auth/seed/CLI paths go
      through it.
    - Migration 108: identity_revision counter and identity_change_log
      maintained by triggers (NOTIFY vh_identity); the daemon polls it every
      second to apply out-of-band changes; a state never replaces a newer one.
    - Batched identity loader: any number of accounts and groups in ~8
      statements, no group member lists, no password hashes; credential checks
      use a dedicated query.
    - FUSE: the caller and vault owner come from memory; deactivated accounts
      are refused (they were not).
    - Vault permission checks no longer load the vault owner from the database;
      API key listing no longer dereferences a missing owner.
    - Contract test: identity writes outside identities::Manager are rejected
      (tools/contracts).
    - HTTP cookie auth: refresh-token row read in one round trip
      (Transactions::read); the owner comes from the row and the canonical
      account (the users JOIN per request is gone); JWT secret cached in
      crypto::secrets::Manager.
  * Previews
    - /preview/batch: index-only readiness in one query per engine
      (Store::status), "failed" for known-bad sources, no artifact decrypts and
      no cache hit/miss accounting for status checks.
    - Derived cache hits: Store::read (one round trip via Transactions::read,
      one open, one decrypt), in-memory hit tracking flushed in batches;
      migration 109 adds cache_index.page_count for PDF renders.
    - Render: single flight per source generation and page; a decode emits all
      missing thumbnail sizes at or below the rendered size; separate
      interactive and background render gates.
    - Disposable artifacts (thumbnails, page renders) skip fsync; the startup
      sweep removes artifact files without rows.
    - Generator version 3: fast IDCT and 4:2:0 for thumbnail sizes, alpha
      composited over white.
    - Web grid requests 256/512 px thumbnails for its tiles; the legacy ws
      share.preview.get renders through the cached, gated pipeline and never
      fetches remote-only bytes.
    - Deferred outputs: an on-demand page-0 render returns the requested size,
      then finishes the smaller thumbnail sizes from the same raster on the
      thumbnail pool while holding the decode's flight.
  * Filesystem
    - fs cache listDir: completeness checked with one statement (direct child
      count, subtree totals) instead of two transactions reloading the
      directory and its subdirectories; parent->children index replaces a scan
      of every cached entry per listing.
    - Directory totals: one recursive statement updates every ancestor (rows
      locked nearest-first) instead of an UPDATE and a parent lookup per level;
      ancestor chains load in one statement; signed size delta in the rename
      re-encrypt path (a shrinking file no longer wraps).
    - Web/API overwrite refreshes the cached ancestor directory totals.
  * Sync
    - rbac::resolver::Vault: sync config/action permissions also come from a
      vault role on the vault (the account's own or a group's), unioned with
      the admin vault globals (#189); ops::conflicts::canResolveIn uses the
      resolver alone. Vault-role roles permissions stay globals-only.
    - Planner: a file whose sides are unchanged since the per-file baseline is
      skipped under every conflict policy, so keep_remote / keep_newest no
      longer re-download a file they downloaded (#190).

